I added `cheapestStart` at the end of `src/tariff.ts`. It tries each day from `fromDay` to `toDay` inclusive. It keeps the first day with the lowest total, so ties go to the earliest, and it returns the day as given.

I couldn't open the file, so I guessed the existing quoting function. I assumed `quoteTotal(boatClass, startDay, nights, pets)` returns a number, and that `0` means no pets. If your function has a different name, argument order or return type, such as an object with a `total` field or a pets flag, you'll need to change that one call. I also assumed `BoatClass` is already defined or imported in the file.
